Introduction of Cypress
1. FrontEnd webBased automation tool
2. Its tool to test modern web based application (New frameworks suchs as reactJS,
	Angular JS uses to build websites)
3. Cypress is capable to test any webbased application which run over browsers..
4. In Cypress, we write testscript in javascript and typescript langugage...
5. Cypress doesnot use any selenium library, architecture using cypress completely     different from slenium 
6. Cypress is an opensource 
		local execution - free
		server based - cloud - paid services
7. Cypress run on node.js (environment)
	
Main Feature in Cypress
1. Time travel --> Capture screenshot at each steps
2. Automatic Wait
3. Consistency (Flaky test)
4. Screenshot and video (bydefault available)
5. Cross browser testing. 		


Cypress Structure
1. e2e - testcases
2. Fixtures - testdata
3. Support - reusable code (custome function)
4. cyress.config.js - global  configuration of cypress (BaseURL, video)


how to run the cypress test from terminal or CMD
1. Open Cypress - npx cypress open
2. to run test from terminal - npx cypress run
    bydefault cypress runs the testscript on electron browser with headless mode (without brower enable on screen)
3. npx cypress run --headed 
4. npx cypress run --headed --browser "browserName"  | npx cypress run --headed -b "browserName"
5. npx cypress run --spec cypress/e2e/open_Applicaitonurl.cy.js --headed --browser chrome
6. viewport 


to enable videocapturing in cypress

const { defineConfig } = require("cypress");

module.exports = defineConfig({
  allowCypressEnv: false,

  e2e: {
    video:true,
    setupNodeEvents(on, config) {
      // implement node event listeners here
      
    },
  },
});

